      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: complete pinned repair validation",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- complete the remaining acceptance criteria from https://github.com/openclaw/clawsweeper/issues/492 after https://github.com/openclaw/clawsweeper/pull/494 landed\n- prove four moving-main review attempts keep one captured base and final synchronization receives one exact validation/review\n- classify a validation failure as external only after the same command reproduces the same normalized diagnostic on an isolated pinned-base checkout\n- prepare dependencies independently inside the pinned checkout; fail closed when safe setup is disabled/fails, dependency inputs changed, or the pinned ref is unavailable\n- preserve repair scope for changed or ambiguous diagnostics, document the final-sync contract, and retain reporter credit here while leaving release-owned changelog files untouched\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe first landed repair pinned the main execution paths and renewed publication credentials, but its moving-base coverage was source-level and its validation path did not deterministically distinguish a genuine pinned-base failure from a repair-induced failure reported in an unchanged file.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pnpm run lint:repair`\n- `pnpm run test:repair` — 713 passed\n- `pnpm run test:coverage:changed` — 100% lines/functions, 88.61% branches\n- `pnpm run format:check`\n- focused built repair/CLI suite — 59 passed\n- source-blind behavior contract — all 6 clauses passed, including invalid-base rejection\n- autoreview — clean; no accepted/actionable findings\n\nHosted proof on the first exact head:\n\n- Linux/Windows CI: https://github.com/openclaw/clawsweeper/actions/runs/29146638078\n- CodeQL: https://github.com/openclaw/clawsweeper/actions/runs/29146638063\n- ClawSweeper review: https://github.com/openclaw/clawsweeper/actions/runs/29146639484\n\nThat live review caught dependency contamination in the first pinned-base checkout implementation. The first follow-up rejected tracked dependency-input changes; exact-head re-review then proved that ignored/generated mutations could still contaminate a shared runtime, and that rejecting all prepared runtimes made the classifier unreachable in the normal path. The final implementation never shares `node_modules`: it installs from pinned inputs inside the detached checkout when setup is enabled, and preserves repair scope when independent setup is unavailable. Integration coverage exercises normal setup followed by a base-identical failure, the requested untracked runtime mutation, unstaged/staged/committed dependency changes, and an unavailable pinned ref.\n\n## Final-head live proof\n\nBuilt `dist/repair`, then exercised its exported setup, validation, pinned reproduction, and classifier against a real temporary Git repository. Both checkouts performed an actual npm install of a committed local dependency; no command or package-manager mocks were used. Redacted output from exact head `8dcf3ff33879e86bd119f3038f015e6392f14965`:\n\n```text\nrepaired_runtime_ready=true\nrepair_validation_failed=true\nisolated_pinned_validation_failed=true\nexternal_blocker=true\nblocker_paths=check.mjs,src/base.ts\nrepair_delta=src/repair.ts\n```\n\nThe diagnostic paths remained base-identical while the only repair delta was `src/repair.ts`, proving the terminal external-blocker boundary after independent pinned-checkout setup.\n\n`pnpm run check` reaches the existing macOS harness failures unchanged from `origin/main`: two Bash 3.2 lowercase-expansion tests and one missing-Corepack fixture. The repair suite and changed-surface gates are green; hosted Linux CI remains the full-suite authority.\n\nCloses https://github.com/openclaw/clawsweeper/issues/492\n",
        "branch": "fix/issue-492-acceptance-gaps",
